</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Butland</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Fisher</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Bowyer</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><source>Men's health: A research agenda and background report</source><year>1998</year><publisher-name>Canberra: Commonwealth Department of Health &#x00026; Aged Care</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schofield</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Connell</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name><name><surname>Walker</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Wood</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Butland</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Understanding men's health and illness: A gender-relations approach to policy, research and practice</article-title><source>J Am Coll Health</source><year>2000</year><volume>48</volume><fpage>247</fpage><lpage>256</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10863868</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lumb</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Why is men's health and well-being policy not implemented in Australia?</article-title><source>International Journal of Men's Health</source><year>2003</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>73</fpage><lpage>88</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.3149/jmh.0201.73</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Edwards</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Men's health: social policy and the new man</article-title><source>Social Alternatives</source><year>1997</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>55</fpage><lpage>